@startuml 02-sequence-consume
title Consume units
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #4F46E5
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #C7D2FE
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF2FF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #4F46E5
skinparam ParticipantFontStyle bold
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #EEF2FF
skinparam ActorBorderColor #4F46E5
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #EEF2FF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #4F46E5
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam NoteBorderColor #F59E0B
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam SequenceGroupHeaderFontColor #334155
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #E0E7FF
skinparam SequenceDividerBorderColor #4F46E5
skinparam TitleFontSize 18

participant "Client app" as Client
participant "API" as API
database "Database" as DB

Client -> API : POST /usage/consume\n{ userId, units, requestId }
API -> DB : seen this requestId before?

alt yes (a retry)
  DB --> API : stored decision
  API --> Client : same decision again\n(nothing consumed twice)
else no (new request)
  API -> DB : lock account + user counters
  API -> API : check the rules\n(user plan and account plan)
  opt all rules pass
    API -> DB : add units to both counters
  end
  API -> DB : save the decision
  API --> Client : accepted or rejected\n+ remaining units
end

note over API, DB
  Everything runs in one transaction,
  so parallel requests can never go over a limit.
end note
@enduml
